                'description' => "Given `n` non-negative integers `height[0], height[1], ..., height[n-1]`, where each represents the height of a bar in an elevation map (each bar has width 1), compute how much water the map can trap after it rains.\n\nWater sits on top of bar `i` up to the height of the shorter of the tallest bar to its left and the tallest bar to its right, minus `height[i]` itself — and only counts when that amount is positive.",
